{"name":"Osso Bucco","hex":"#ad9769","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"osso bucco","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of osso buco."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/osso_bucco"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ossobuco","blocks":[{"text":"Ossobuco or osso buco, also known as ossobuco alla milanese, is a specialty of Lombard cuisine of cross-cut veal shanks braised with vegetables, white wine, and broth. It is often garnished with gremolada and traditionally served with either risotto alla milanese or polenta, depending on the regional variation. The marrow from the hole in the bone is a prized delicacy and the defining feature of the dish."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Ossobuco.jpg/330px-Ossobuco.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ossobuco","wikidata":"Q1057256"},{"title":"Bucco","blocks":[{"text":"Bucco is a genus of birds in the puffbird family Bucconidae. Birds in the genus are native to the Americas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Collared_Puffbird.jpg/330px-Collared_Puffbird.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bucco","wikidata":"Q611069"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Veal-shank.jpg/500px-Veal-shank.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Veal-shank.jpg/500px-Veal-shank.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Veal shank","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVeal-shank.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Redaktionsvortreffen_EuT_2_ossobuco_16.04.2011_22-59-12.2011_22-59-12.jpg/500px-Redaktionsvortreffen_EuT_2_ossobuco_16.04.2011_22-59-12.2011_22-59-